1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,870
You're looking at a British admiral his

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:04,020
own country shot in 1757.

3
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:06,420
The judges begged for mercy.

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:07,880
So why did he die?

5
00:00:08,197 --> 00:00:11,087
Admiral John Byng. In 1756,

6
00:00:11,517 --> 00:00:13,497
Britain sends him to save the island of

7
00:00:13,497 --> 00:00:14,767
Minorca from the French,

8
00:00:15,197 --> 00:00:16,357
with ships in poor repair,

9
00:00:16,357 --> 00:00:18,367
and hundreds of sailors short.

10
00:00:18,646 --> 00:00:20,256
Off the island, the fleets clash.

11
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:21,926
His line falls apart,

12
00:00:21,926 --> 00:00:23,696
and his ships take heavy damage.

13
00:00:24,026 --> 00:00:25,896
He sails back to Gibraltar for repairs.

14
00:00:26,626 --> 00:00:27,316
Minorca falls.

15
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:29,667
In London, the government prints an edited

16
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:32,187
version of his report that makes him look

17
00:00:32,187 --> 00:00:35,277
like a coward. Crowds burn him in effigy.

18
00:00:35,464 --> 00:00:37,654
His court martial clears him of cowardice.

19
00:00:37,964 --> 00:00:39,794
But it rules he did not "do his utmost".

20
00:00:40,304 --> 00:00:42,374
Under the law, that carries one sentence:

21
00:00:42,764 --> 00:00:43,074
death.

22
00:00:43,464 --> 00:00:45,274
The judges ask the King for mercy.

23
00:00:45,644 --> 00:00:46,594
The King says no.

24
00:00:46,992 --> 00:00:51,632
March 14, 1757. On the deck of HMS Monarch,

25
00:00:51,632 --> 00:00:52,732
with the fleet watching,

26
00:00:52,732 --> 00:00:54,322
Byng kneels on a cushion.

27
00:00:54,732 --> 00:00:56,002
He drops his handkerchief.

28
00:00:56,352 --> 00:00:57,282
The Marines fire.

29
00:00:57,883 --> 00:01:00,143
Voltaire mocked it: "In this country,

30
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,103
it is good to kill an admiral from time

31
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,253
to time, to encourage the others."

32
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:07,720
In 2007, his family asked for a pardon.

33
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:10,930
The government refused. His tomb still says

34
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:12,780
he fell "a martyr to political persecution".

35
00:01:13,346 --> 00:01:15,666
Scapegoat, or justice? Tell me below,

36
00:01:15,666 --> 00:01:17,416
and follow Buried Chronicles.

